        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To evaluate a large exponent, we first write out the power using multiplication signs as usual. Then, we calculate the product by splitting it into groups of two-digit multiplications, before calculating the resulting product. </p>",
            "readable_text": "To evaluate a large exponent, we first write out the power using multiplication signs as usual. Then, we calculate the product by splitting it into groups of two-digit multiplications, before calculating the resulting product.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, let&#x27;s evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^4.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, let's evaluate [MATH: 2^4.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we write\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we write\n[MATH: 4]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2 \\times 2 = 4,]</span> we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} \\times \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} = {\\color{blue}4} \\times {\\color{blue}4}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Since [MATH: 2 \\times 2 = 4,] we have\n[MATH: \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} \\times \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} = {\\color{blue}4} \\times {\\color{blue}4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Finally, we work out <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4\\times 4.]</span>\nSince <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4\\times 4=16,]</span> we conclude that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^4=16.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Finally, we work out [MATH: 4\\times 4.]\nSince [MATH: 4\\times 4=16,] we conclude that [MATH: 2^4=16.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nTo evaluate a large exponent, we first write out the power using multiplication signs as usual. Then, we calculate the product by splitting it into groups of two-digit multiplications, before calculating the resulting product.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's evaluate [MATH: 2^4.]\n\nContent:\nFirst, we write\n[MATH: 4]\n\nContent:\nSince [MATH: 2 \\times 2 = 4,] we have\n[MATH: \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} \\times \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} = {\\color{blue}4} \\times {\\color{blue}4}.]\n\nContent:\nFinally, we work out [MATH: 4\\times 4.]\nSince [MATH: 4\\times 4=16,] we conclude that [MATH: 2^4=16.]"
      },
