        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 220^2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Evaluate [MATH: 220^2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 220^2,]</span> we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span></p><p>Then, we work out <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 220 \\times 220.]</span></p><p>First, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 220|\u27f6220; 220|\u27f6220]</span></p><p>We can see that there are <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span> zeros in total.</p><p>Next, we multiply the non-zero parts:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2|2; \u00d7|0|0|2|2; 0|4|4; +|4|4|0; 4|8|4]</span></p><p>Finally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}484}{\\color{blue}00}= 48,400]</span></p><p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 220^2  =   48,400.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To evaluate [MATH: 220^2,] we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n[MATH: 2]\n\nThen, we work out [MATH: 220 \\times 220.]\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n[MATH: 220|\u27f6220; 220|\u27f6220]\n\nWe can see that there are [MATH: 2] zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n[MATH: 2|2; \u00d7|0|0|2|2; 0|4|4; +|4|4|0; 4|8|4]\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros:\n[MATH: {\\color{red}484}{\\color{blue}00}= 48,400]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 220^2 = 48,400.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: 220^2.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo evaluate [MATH: 220^2,] we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n[MATH: 2]\n\nThen, we work out [MATH: 220 \\times 220.]\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n[MATH: 220|\u27f6220; 220|\u27f6220]\n\nWe can see that there are [MATH: 2] zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n[MATH: 2|2; \u00d7|0|0|2|2; 0|4|4; +|4|4|0; 4|8|4]\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros:\n[MATH: {\\color{red}484}{\\color{blue}00}= 48,400]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: 220^2 = 48,400.]"
      },
